  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Use only set-3 irregulars as the key: blew, broke, built, chose, drank, drew, drove, fell, flew, froze, grew, heard, kept, rode, sang, spoke, stood, woke, wore, wrote.",
      "Every wrong choice must be the same verb in a fake -ed form, a present or -s form, an -ing form, or a past participle.",
      "Never put a real past from another verb in the choice row. That makes two past answers.",
      "Tier 1 wrong choices should look obviously regular, like flied or growed.",
      "Tier 3 must use the past participle as the near miss, like chosen or driven, plus one fake -ed form.",
      "Keep stems in kid places: school, home, food, pets, play, family, or weather. No brands and no real names."
    ]
